            </staff>
            <div xml:id="m-2f641ac8-73ca-4584-92b6-61b1792227ac">
              <lg xml:id="m-aae70d70-10ff-45d5-a030-2a32f9f0ef82">
                <l xml:id="m-66718ba4-8a5f-4c76-901c-87314376fae6" facs="#m-945bdada-0d54-4fcd-a2c2-10b0c76142a7" label="text-like">Rules for Interpretation.</l><l xml:id="m-0ac0b478-55f2-4ab3-bbf4-2946a3c9bede" facs="#m-fc62fc15-49ca-44f5-9238-a29a4fc4278f" label="ambiguous">XXI.</l><l xml:id="m-4fb18382-c747-4e88-a6e8-ba8360f8f166" facs="#m-f29fad10-9b07-4611-93c4-e1af48fa33b8" label="text-like">Ist form: always with a vertical episema under the 2nd note:</l><l xml:id="m-1531c662-832a-42a4-a31d-cdd09059658c" facs="#m-db88c834-9829-4cc1-a5d3-9fe7619379f5" label="ambiguous">Salicus</l><l xml:id="m-3f2a14e0-9550-4ba4-b9f6-852792afc816" facs="#m-d432e738-2b33-4c4d-8ff1-64880f70863e" label="text-like">2nd form: with the two first notes on the same degree: (a)</l><l xml:id="m-32794284-dfe4-4428-b1cf-508bc088e854" facs="#m-d7369500-a587-4d19-8ccd-071e4dd66a91" label="ambiguous">2Descending:</l><l xml:id="m-eb85ada2-2cf9-4e07-a013-e0df98ad60a5" facs="#m-d096a8e0-ba47-4031-8c93-fdcadda8c1d2" label="ambiguous">Climacus</l><l xml:id="m-5351fdba-5eb8-4f21-a83c-1406a9ffb1cb" facs="#m-798e2097-dfd7-4f24-b838-39a63d9c501a" label="text-like">3. with the 2nd note of the group higher than the two others:</l><l xml:id="m-02563a29-18a9-4aa8-8f4a-48ecb47f28ef" facs="#m-8f3b7e18-3ae4-4357-bb93-84f82cc6f281" label="ambiguous">Torculus</l><l xml:id="m-16bb0f4c-328e-485f-ab2b-dfc3bc0f5a0f" facs="#m-368da61b-1fe3-4779-aa60-b4149fa14102" label="ambiguous">(</l><l xml:id="m-a5056169-d593-46f8-b8b0-36cf2ce794e3" facs="#m-9137d61b-902c-4ed2-a5ec-9b7eff98102f" label="text-like">Lower than the two others:</l><l xml:id="m-585662e5-0c61-4e3d-9123-c25a442cd284" facs="#m-bfdf0104-0076-47e3-b69b-36758cd7ea2c" label="ambiguous">Porrectus</l><l xml:id="m-b28454d3-b247-4f9a-8a3c-688a7d307bf5" facs="#m-b3d66095-9c30-4ea4-bb57-462656cf7a20" label="text-like">4. On the same degree:</l><l xml:id="m-381596b6-9862-4356-9656-ced7123939f2" facs="#m-1bb25ce1-238a-4b87-9270-6bfb7c0db34c" label="ambiguous">Tristropha</l><l xml:id="m-abd4dc7d-b165-4844-8842-fabec0ff6746" facs="#m-4b2e93b1-0caa-4348-9a78-30e511546c72" label="text-like">D. — COMPOUND NEUMS OR GROUPS OF MORE THAN THREE NOTES.</l><l xml:id="m-582f670f-aabc-4594-a271-168b81d02919" facs="#m-13eec964-076b-4bb1-a498-c79a977aa568" label="text-like">Pes or</l><l xml:id="m-bd91349f-2d21-4049-a8e5-01e16ba4c931" facs="#m-7e62ea27-4eac-41cd-a312-89a49ca04b73" label="ambiguous">Pomects!</l><l xml:id="m-fbf86474-2f52-4de4-af5d-620618a9c337" facs="#m-61ba3d3f-d7a9-473e-b8ff-02e260fcbc8d" label="ambiguous">Podatus HI</l><l xml:id="m-d25cc8b1-0bdd-44bf-9404-af3cda361f90" facs="#m-202fef2e-5125-4b29-b33e-488d181cc0c5" label="ambiguous" /><l xml:id="m-afeae372-d083-475c-9b1a-ec3b13c79d70" facs="#m-09a88f3f-bafe-4d1c-9063-fe9971ddcb9a" label="ambiguous">flexus</l><l xml:id="m-8890997d-07ec-4ca5-ac3e-aa413a3ee856" facs="#m-82e2128d-3562-4832-8ca6-71733525614d" label="ambiguous">sub¬</l><l xml:id="m-56fe5b28-f17a-4a33-9430-0ad61668f0ea" facs="#m-ef3fe0a7-0c84-415f-9eff-b7d9c240f267" label="ambiguous">bipunctis</l><l xml:id="m-d0388a0b-5ced-4a8c-8bd7-c66cbeff4c06" facs="#m-0ce2e5bb-e498-4637-8c08-386345c69425" label="ambiguous">Salicus</l><l xml:id="m-e7ac8665-9413-4a56-8c0e-a8dbcf29912d" facs="#m-3af72283-b1e4-4db0-8f7e-ada72cde3ab3" label="ambiguous">2E</l><l xml:id="m-8e94e595-1925-4724-bb79-c968f201bce4" facs="#m-506a9f59-ad78-4851-a061-4b32e396e984" label="ambiguous">Torculus</l><l xml:id="m-4c2b5d71-a73c-479f-9fc8-807aeeaab4fb" facs="#m-8adc884e-59e8-486b-a265-b8fbac76bf0c" label="ambiguous">flexus</l><l xml:id="m-225680dc-02be-4aca-8b6c-e5b2c6af944f" facs="#m-e61509b7-a000-4ddf-8960-24edf6d1cdf2" label="ambiguous">resupinus</l><l xml:id="m-f0d08c08-352f-4f4a-ae43-1985b7a91c05" facs="#m-5fc977f5-4699-4c48-b75c-13c36ec8f318" label="ambiguous">Climacus</l><l xml:id="m-a95292f2-7a8b-4020-8492-3c2347729c3f" facs="#m-43f210f3-e549-491f-b2f4-01ace84927ec" label="ambiguous">Scandicus</l><l xml:id="m-88094439-55c1-4ac5-bf36-d0e387b87c86" facs="#m-a8ca74e8-873b-4aee-ac1b-42efdc8fd544" label="ambiguous">6</l><l xml:id="m-cf903b5e-87b6-488e-bfa4-e8966c368045" facs="#m-6793cbf6-504b-4174-a1e7-fce7c8d2827d" label="ambiguous">flexus</l><l xml:id="m-abdd5032-d6d3-4ec7-a53c-3363054dbe0f" facs="#m-66fff4e7-1bc9-4488-9e7e-6ee08be92f69" label="ambiguous">resupinus</l><l xml:id="m-6b5bbed2-92ca-4757-a566-eb04ad81f4b7" facs="#m-52a68cb9-f675-4907-a82a-79f41cd1c14e" label="text-like">1a) For practical purposes this second form of Salicus will be treated as a pressus (sce note on</l><l xml:id="m-3827784a-18a6-494d-b8d4-96cce6504cc9" facs="#m-80ae5960-6b78-4ff9-ae3e-258be164d579" label="text-like">this group)</l></lg>
            </div>
          </section>
        </score>
      </mdiv>
    </body>
  </music>
</mei>